<article class="env-lemma" id="0E3R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E3R">Lemma <span data-tag="0E3R">90.20.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{H}$ be maps of categories cofibred in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda $. If </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$, $\mathcal{G}$ are deformation categories 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the map $T\mathcal{F} \to T\mathcal{G}$ is surjective, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{H}$ is smooth. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ is smooth. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $A' \to A$ be a small extension in $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda $ and let $x \in \mathcal{F}(A)$ with image $y \in \mathcal{G}(A)$. Assume there is a lift $y' \in \mathcal{G}(A')$. According to Lemma <a href="/tag/0DYP" data-tag="0DYP">90.20.3</a> all we have to do is check that $x$ has a lift too. Take the image $z' \in \mathcal{H}(A')$ of $y'$. Since $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{H}$ is smooth, there is an $x' \in \mathcal{F}(A')$ mapping to both $x \in \mathcal{F}(A)$ and $z' \in \mathcal{H}(A')$, see Definition <a href="/tag/06HG" data-tag="06HG">90.8.1</a>. This finishes the proof. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>